    {
      "id": "cluster-bones-under-new-node",
      "name": "ClusterBonesUnderNewNode",
      "category": "GeometryCollectionClusteringUtility",
      "signature": "ClusterBonesUnderNewNode(Geometry Collection, Insert At Index, Selected Bones, Calc New Local Transform, Validate)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Geometry Collection",
          "type": "FGeometryCollection*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Insert At Index",
          "type": "Int"
        },
        {
          "name": "Selected Bones",
          "type": "TArray<int32>&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Calc New Local Transform",
          "type": "Bool"
        },
        {
          "name": "Validate",
          "type": "Bool",
          "default": "true"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "public : int32",
      "docs": "Creates a cluster in the node hierarchy by re-parenting the Selected Bones off a new node in the hierarchy\nIt makes more sense to think that the Selected Bones are all at the same level in the hierarchy however\nit will re-parent multiple levels at the InsertAtIndex location bone\ne.g. if you have a flat chunk hierarchy after performing Voronoi fracturing\nL0         Root\n|\n----------\n|  |  |  |\nL1     A  B  C  D\nCluster A & B at insertion point A, results in\nL0         Root\n|\n----------\n|     |  |\nL1     E     C  D\n|\n----\n|  |\nL2    A  B\nNode E has no geometry of its own, only a transform by which to control A & B as a single unit\n@return Index of the New Node"
    },
